.fill.justify.offset 5.rightmargin 70.pagesize 72.m1 3.m2 2.m3 2.m4 5.ec \.header /Mesg/Utility/Mesg.footer /Page #//Printed (%)/.in +5.define topic.bold.in -5$1 $2 $3 $4 $5.in +5.en.define endtopic.en.define noform.nojustify.nofill.en.define noformend.justify.fill.en.! Manual created with MWB.! END-OF-MACRO.topic NAMEMesg - Change status flags in /dd/SYS/utmp.endtopic.topic SYNOPSIS.noformmesg <flags>.noformend.endtopic.topic DESCRIPTION	The file /dd/SYS/utmp supports some (ten) user defined flagsthat can be used by several programs. A flag is considerd as on if it iswritten in uppercase or off when in lowercase (or not present). Twoflags are pre definied. The `V` and `M` flag. `V` stands for visiable;the user can only see these user who has this flag ON using the whocommand (every user in group zero can see everyone.) The `M` stands forreceiving messages ON or OFF. This is used by the program.ulmsgthats mostly called by.ulmmenua user interface for BBS etc. To hange theses flags just call .ulmesgwith the flags to switch the option on (upper case) or off (lower case.).endtopic.topic FILES.noform/dd/SYS/utmp.in +3The flags for each logged on user are stored here..in -3.noformend.endtopic.topic EXAMPLES.noformmesg V.in +3Switches visiable on..in -3.noformend.endtopic.topic SEE ALSOLogon in the TOP Munich Release for default values in the password file..endtopic.topic AUTHOR.in 0.ce 4Ulrich DessauerKerschensteinerstr. 45, D-8034 GermeringVoice: +49 89 8417811E-Mail: ..!{chiuur|doitcr}!nitmar!ud.endtopic